> f(x: f32 in 0..1) = x * 0.5
> intatomic f
intatomic f under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of 0.5x, at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  no exact fixed point: x is not on a binary grid (only integers, binary constants, + - * and powers of two keep one)
  -> not rewritten: `tol T` allows a rounded scaling (T: absolute error on the sum)
> g(x: u32 in 0..255) = f32(x) * 0.5
> intatomic g count 100
intatomic g under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of 0.5f32(x), at most 100 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  the addend is k 2^-1 with |k| <= 255, exactly: every leaf is an integer or a binary constant, the
  operations keep the grid, and no f32 value on the way needs more than 24 bits, so none rounds
  the sum of 100 of them is at most 25500 2^-1: it fits 32 bits (25500 < 2^31), so the integer sum is the exact sum
  the float sum would be exact too (it stays within 24 bits): the two agree bit for bit, in every order
  the integer addend: i32(x)
  -> atomic_add_shared(cell, i32(x)): addend and atomic cost 6.625 against 28.25 (-76.5%)
     the cell is an i32 holding the sum times 2^1; every other access of it changes too: a store of v
     stores i32(v * 2^1), a read is f32(cell) * 2^-1 (a conversion and a multiply: 4 a read)
  defined g_ia: the atomic's old value read back as a float
> h(x: f32 in -1..1) = x + 1.0
> intatomic h tol 1e-3
intatomic h under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of x + 1, at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  no exact fixed point: x is not on a binary grid (only integers, binary constants, + - * and powers of two keep one)
  -> not rewritten: the addend's range is not known (give its parameters ranges)
> intatomic h tol 1e-3 global
intatomic h under gt1030: a global float atomic add of x + 1, at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 138.75, an integer one 50
  no exact fixed point: x is not on a binary grid (only integers, binary constants, + - * and powers of two keep one)
  -> not rewritten: the addend's range is not known (give its parameters ranges)
